1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,280
Gloss Lint checks doc comments and module pages against a project's house style.

2
00:00:06,030 --> 00:00:09,130
Take a comment that begins with, this method records it.

3
00:00:09,490 --> 00:00:12,150
Gloss Lint reports it in the format a compiler uses.

4
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:18,230
The file, the line, the column, the severity, then the fix, and the rule code in

5
00:00:18,230 --> 00:00:18,530
brackets.

6
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:25,180
Because it looks like compiler output, Xcode, continuous integration and a commit hook can all show

7
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:25,820
it as it is.

8
00:00:27,833 --> 00:00:29,913
The Linter is the entry point.

9
00:00:30,173 --> 00:00:33,193
It runs the Rules over every declaration it reads.

10
00:00:33,943 --> 00:00:37,463
Each rule is a single teachable failure, with a code.

11
00:00:37,703 --> 00:00:39,183
A missing doc comment.

12
00:00:39,483 --> 00:00:41,643
A summary that opens with this method.

13
00:00:41,963 --> 00:00:45,503
A function that returns a value but has no returns entry.

14
00:00:46,253 --> 00:00:52,953
Every finding becomes a Diagnostic, which knows its file, line, column, rule and message,

15
00:00:53,193 --> 00:00:55,093
and renders itself as one line.

16
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:03,420
Each project sets its own house style, in a file named style dot json inside its

17
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:04,060
gloss folder.

18
00:01:04,650 --> 00:01:07,550
A rule can be an error, a warning, or off.

19
00:01:07,830 --> 00:01:11,530
A prefix such as summary star sets a whole family at once.

20
00:01:11,910 --> 00:01:16,690
Some paths can be excluded, and the style says which declarations owe a doc comment.

21
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:22,640
With no file, every rule is an error, and every declaration but the private ones needs

22
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,240
a doc comment.

23
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:28,100
A key gloss doesn't know is an error, so a typo never leaves a rule quietly

24
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:28,420
on.

25
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,420
Nothing in Gloss Lint knows the contract model.

26
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:38,320
So a team can lint without the app, and the app can read docs without the

27
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:38,560
lint.

28
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:41,730
The one thing that crosses is the Assessment.

29
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:44,530
It is what the views take from the linter.

30
00:01:45,110 --> 00:01:46,990
That is all the module does.

31
00:01:47,230 --> 00:01:51,270
It checks the prose, and says so in a line any tool can read.
